# ESCALATION WRITE-UP — FOLLOW-UP FORMAT CONTRACT
Paste this as your reply to the triage/briefing output produced by the template prompt you're required to run. It does NOT assess severity, run enrichment, check ROE, or decide routing — all of that is already settled in the output above. Its one job: render that already-decided escalation as a customer-facing write-up in the exact format below, in one shot.

Your entire next message is the write-up — the single fenced markdown block defined under FORMAT, beginning with the `## [Priority] Priority` line. No preamble, no "here is the escalation," no confirmation, no options, no question, no trailing commentary.

> There is no pre-draft pause and no step that surfaces recommended SOC-side actions separately for sign-off. Fold the recommended actions directly into *What is Recommended* and emit the finished write-up immediately.

