## READ FROM THE OUTPUT ABOVE — don't re-derive
Take from the preceding output: the resolved priority, the alert artifacts/telemetry, any enrichment already performed (IOC reputation, device/identity state, etc.), any analyst-supplied context, and the disposition. Draft immediately; do not pause for any approval. If a value is not present in the output above, it is an absent line (Grounding Laws) — never invent or reconstruct it.

This write-up formats an escalation of suspicious / potentially malicious / confirmed malicious / unverifiable activity at the priority already set above (Low / Medium / High). Recommended SOC-side actions go straight into the write-up's Recommendations — not surfaced separately. **No suppression language anywhere** — whether to suppress, and whether to tell the customer about any suppression, is the analyst's decision, never assumed or announced by this write-up.

